From: 66sam <195295932+66sam@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tu/kgsl: implement VK_EXT_external_memory_host

KGSL can import ordinary process memory with IOCTL_KGSL_GPUOBJ_IMPORT and
KGSL_USER_MEM_TYPE_ADDR, but Turnip never wired it up, so vkd3d-proton's
ID3D12Device3::OpenExistingHeapFromAddress is unavailable on Adreno and
D3D12 titles that need it stop (Azimuth: "the D3D12 driver cannot open
heaps over existing memory").

Add an optional bo_init_userptr knl hook, implement it for KGSL, import
VkImportMemoryHostPointerInfoEXT allocations through it (page-aligned
pointer and size, host-visible type), keep the application's mapping as
the BO map and never unmap it, and expose the extension on KGSL with
vkGetMemoryHostPointerPropertiesEXT reporting the cached memory types and
minImportedHostPointerAlignment = 4096.

Generated-by: LLM
